{"id": "features-look", "window": ["2016-10-24", "2022-12-30"], "sessions": 1584, "intro": ["1,584 London sessions (2016-10-24 to 2022-12-30) on a 1-minute bid/ask mid grid of the 7 USD majors, split into a leave-own-out dollar (the other six) and each pair's own move, β from the prior 20 sessions only. 2023 onwards is not looked at.", "The dollar explains 56-58% of EURUSD, AUDUSD and NZDUSD 5-minute variance, 37-43% of GBPUSD, USDCAD and USDCHF, and 22% of USDJPY. A dollar path from a random other session explains about 0.5%: the split is real, not chance.", "It is not fixed: GBPUSD went from about 20% dollar (2016-2019, Brexit) to 56% (2022); USDJPY from 31-34% (2016-17) to 7-11% (2018-20). But day to day it is persistent (0.51-0.76 correlation with yesterday's share), so the open knows roughly which kind of day to expect.", "Correlation rises with vol, but only a little: 0.40 on the calmest tenth of days to 0.50-0.54 on the loudest, while 'only the dollar got louder' would give 0.87. On loud days the dollar's variance grows 8x and each pair's own variance 6x. Sorted by yesterday's vol the rise is smaller (0.44 to about 0.48-0.52).", "Own moves reverse slightly at 5 minutes (slope -0.023), but skipping one minute halves it (-0.013): about half is quote timing. Dollar moves do not continue (slope -0.001 to +0.006). After the biggest own moves the pair gives back 0.002σ; the round-trip spread is 0.036σ, 17 times more.", "Traps measured: a cross rebuilt from its own legs has R² 0.99 (the cross itself), against 0.01-0.05 for the dollar; putting the pair inside its own dollar basket adds 11-17 points of fake common share.", "Gold is 22% dollar (β about -1); NQ and SPX 12% overall, near 0 in 2016-2019 and about 24-27% in 2022.", "What it means: the split is a strong, stable description of RISK (book stops, which currency is moving) and gives no intraday fade or follow signal by itself."], "charts": [{"type": "groups", "title": "How much of each major's 5-minute variance is the dollar", "names": ["Dollar share, point-in-time β", "Same-day fit (in-sample)", "Wrong-day dollar (benchmark)"], "unit": "share of variance", "note": "Dollar = average of the OTHER six majors (leave-own-out), USD-signed; β from the prior 20 sessions only. Same-day fit = the best possible β for that session (in-sample). Benchmark: the same-day fit against a dollar path from a random OTHER session, what 'no link' looks like (about 0.005 from chance alone).", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "values": [0.5616, 0.5504, 0.0055]}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "values": [0.3961, 0.3933, 0.0053]}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "values": [0.5751, 0.5448, 0.0052]}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "values": [0.5705, 0.5446, 0.0053]}, {"label": "USDCAD", "values": [0.3734, 0.3627, 0.0058]}, {"label": "USDCHF", "values": [0.4258, 0.4083, 0.0054]}, {"label": "USDJPY", "values": [0.2163, 0.2049, 0.0051]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Dollar share at 5 minutes, with 95% date-block intervals", "unit": "share of variance", "ref": 0, "note": "Stationary date-block bootstrap (block 20 sessions, 2,000 draws). Benchmark: 0 for no common move.", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "value": 0.5616, "lo": 0.5234, "hi": 0.5974}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "value": 0.3961, "lo": 0.3404, "hi": 0.4487}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "value": 0.5751, "lo": 0.52, "hi": 0.631}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "value": 0.5705, "lo": 0.5217, "hi": 0.6178}, {"label": "USDCAD", "value": 0.3734, "lo": 0.3245, "hi": 0.4249}, {"label": "USDCHF", "value": 0.4258, "lo": 0.3909, "hi": 0.4605}, {"label": "USDJPY", "value": 0.2163, "lo": 0.1519, "hi": 0.2776}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Year by year: dollar share of 5-minute variance", "unit": "share of variance", "xlabel": "year", "note": "Stability look. 2016 is late October to December only. A flat line means the split is a stable property of the pair.", "series": [{"name": "EURUSD", "points": [[2016, 0.4998], [2017, 0.4947], [2018, 0.6006], [2019, 0.49], [2020, 0.5226], [2021, 0.611], [2022, 0.6104]]}, {"name": "GBPUSD", "points": [[2016, 0.2057], [2017, 0.2204], [2018, 0.3741], [2019, 0.192], [2020, 0.3922], [2021, 0.5058], [2022, 0.5576]]}, {"name": "USDCAD", "points": [[2016, 0.1752], [2017, 0.2493], [2018, 0.3311], [2019, 0.1874], [2020, 0.3659], [2021, 0.4606], [2022, 0.54]]}, {"name": "USDJPY", "points": [[2016, 0.311], [2017, 0.3377], [2018, 0.1055], [2019, 0.0657], [2020, 0.0976], [2021, 0.1937], [2022, 0.2677]]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Dollar share by sampling interval (the Epps effect)", "unit": "share of variance", "xlabel": "minutes per return", "note": "Correlation measured on very short returns is biased low because quotes update at different moments. Benchmark: a flat line (no Epps). The rise from 1 to 60 minutes is the size of the bias.", "series": [{"name": "EURUSD", "points": [[1, 0.5361], [5, 0.5616], [15, 0.57], [60, 0.5773]]}, {"name": "GBPUSD", "points": [[1, 0.3736], [5, 0.3961], [15, 0.4113], [60, 0.4237]]}, {"name": "USDCAD", "points": [[1, 0.3501], [5, 0.3734], [15, 0.3786], [60, 0.3825]]}, {"name": "USDJPY", "points": [[1, 0.2043], [5, 0.2163], [15, 0.2234], [60, 0.2134]]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Two traps: a cross rebuilt from its own legs, and a pair inside its own factor", "unit": "R² at 5 minutes", "ref": 0, "note": "A cross's 'common move' built from its legs is the cross itself (R² ≈ 0.99): triangular arbitrage, not information. The dollar cancels out of a cross (R² ≈ 0.02-0.03). Including the pair in its own dollar basket adds 10-14 points of fake common share (bar = incl. itself; the whisker's low end = leave-own-out).", "rows": [{"label": "EURGBP vs its own legs (EURUSD−GBPUSD)", "value": 0.9882}, {"label": "EURGBP vs the dollar", "value": 0.0116}, {"label": "EURJPY vs its own legs (EURUSD+USDJPY)", "value": 0.993}, {"label": "EURJPY vs the dollar", "value": 0.0477}, {"label": "EURUSD: dollar incl. itself / leave-own-out", "value": 0.6643, "lo": 0.5555, "hi": 0.6643}, {"label": "USDJPY: dollar incl. itself / leave-own-out", "value": 0.3092, "lo": 0.1748, "hi": 0.3092}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Does correlation rise when vol rises? Sorted by the day's own vol", "unit": "mean pairwise correlation (7 majors, 5-min)", "xlabel": "within-year vol decile", "note": "Pooled = one correlation from all 5-min bars in the decile (deciles within each year). Benchmarks: 'only the dollar's variance rose' (Forbes-Rigobon: one-factor model with calm-decile loadings and own variances and this decile's dollar variance, shifted to start at the observed calm value) and 'structure unchanged' (flat at the calm value). From calm to loudest decile the dollar's variance grows 8.1x and the pairs' own variance 5.7x, so correlation rises only a little. Sorting on the same day's vol is itself a conditioning bias; the yesterday-sorted line is the one known at the open.", "series": [{"name": "Pooled, observed", "points": [[1, 0.3952], [2, 0.4153], [3, 0.4459], [4, 0.4586], [5, 0.4681], [6, 0.4659], [7, 0.4962], [8, 0.5137], [9, 0.5382], [10, 0.5046]]}, {"name": "Pooled, sorted by YESTERDAY's vol", "points": [[1, 0.4417], [2, 0.4284], [3, 0.4868], [4, 0.4862], [5, 0.5113], [6, 0.4747], [7, 0.505], [8, 0.5206], [9, 0.5108], [10, 0.4801]]}, {"name": "Only dollar variance rose (FR)", "points": [[1, 0.3952], [2, 0.4685], [3, 0.5163], [4, 0.5434], [5, 0.5738], [6, 0.5959], [7, 0.6283], [8, 0.6608], [9, 0.7025], [10, 0.784]]}, {"name": "Structure unchanged (calm)", "points": [[1, 0.3952], [2, 0.3952], [3, 0.3952], [4, 0.3952], [5, 0.3952], [6, 0.3952], [7, 0.3952], [8, 0.3952], [9, 0.3952], [10, 0.3952]]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Year by year: average correlation of the 7 majors", "unit": "mean pairwise correlation (5-min, USD-signed)", "xlabel": "year", "note": "Pooled over the year vs the mean of daily values. A gap between them means correlation moves inside the year.", "series": [{"name": "Pooled", "points": [[2016, 0.4148], [2017, 0.4441], [2018, 0.4509], [2019, 0.3471], [2020, 0.451], [2021, 0.5471], [2022, 0.5916]]}, {"name": "Mean of daily", "points": [[2016, 0.4547], [2017, 0.4272], [2018, 0.4526], [2019, 0.3568], [2020, 0.475], [2021, 0.5446], [2022, 0.5699]]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Is a day's move mostly the dollar or mostly the pair? (open to 22:00, all 7 majors)", "names": ["Real dollar", "Wrong-day dollar (benchmark)"], "unit": "share of pair-days", "note": "Dollar share of the day's move = c²/(c²+e²), c = β × the dollar's day move, e = the rest. Real days pile up at both ends; the benchmark shows what 'no link' looks like.", "rows": [{"label": "0.0-0.1", "values": [0.25, 0.3463]}, {"label": "0.1-0.2", "values": [0.0947, 0.1307]}, {"label": "0.2-0.3", "values": [0.0697, 0.1]}, {"label": "0.3-0.4", "values": [0.0618, 0.0755]}, {"label": "0.4-0.5", "values": [0.0607, 0.0622]}, {"label": "0.5-0.6", "values": [0.0528, 0.0573]}, {"label": "0.6-0.7", "values": [0.0585, 0.0489]}, {"label": "0.7-0.8", "values": [0.0705, 0.0458]}, {"label": "0.8-0.9", "values": [0.0818, 0.0456]}, {"label": "0.9-1.0", "values": [0.1994, 0.0878]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Is today's dollar share known at the open?", "names": ["vs yesterday's", "vs last 20 sessions' mean", "Shuffled days (benchmark)"], "unit": "correlation of daily 5-min dollar share", "note": "If the split is persistent, the morning knows which kind of day it is likely to be.", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "values": [0.5178, 0.5677, -0.0179]}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "values": [0.759, 0.809, 0.0156]}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "values": [0.7276, 0.7429, 0.0097]}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "values": [0.6762, 0.7099, 0.0068]}, {"label": "USDCAD", "values": [0.6958, 0.7395, -0.007]}, {"label": "USDCHF", "values": [0.5135, 0.5485, -0.0492]}, {"label": "USDJPY", "values": [0.6285, 0.5831, 0.0049]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "What follows a move, 5-minute blocks: slope of next block on this block", "unit": "slope (≈ autocorrelation)", "ref": 0, "note": "Negative = reverses, positive = continues. 'Skip 1 min' and 'bid only' are the quote-bounce checks; 'shuffled' pairs a block with a block from another session (the null). 'Dollar now → own next' > 0 means the pair lags the dollar (stale quotes).", "rows": [{"label": "Own, next block", "value": -0.0225, "lo": -0.0275, "hi": -0.0177}, {"label": "Own, skip 1 min", "value": -0.0125, "lo": -0.0175, "hi": -0.0074}, {"label": "Own, bid quotes only", "value": -0.0239, "lo": -0.029, "hi": -0.0191}, {"label": "Raw pair (no split)", "value": -0.0105, "lo": -0.0142, "hi": -0.0067}, {"label": "Dollar factor", "value": -0.0012, "lo": -0.0065, "hi": 0.0044}, {"label": "Own vs wrong-day dollar", "value": -0.0064, "lo": -0.0102, "hi": -0.0024}, {"label": "Dollar now → own next", "value": 0.0031, "lo": 0.0017, "hi": 0.0044}, {"label": "Shuffled (null)", "value": -0.0002, "lo": -0.0016, "hi": 0.0012}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Own-move reversal by pair (adjacent blocks)", "names": ["5 min", "15 min", "60 min"], "unit": "slope of next own move on this own move", "note": "Benchmark: a block paired with the same clock time on a random other session. That null is about 0 at 5 and 15 minutes (interval ±0.003) but +0.007 [+0.002, +0.013] at 60 minutes, a time-of-day pattern; read 60-minute values against it, not against 0.", "rows": [{"label": "EURUSD", "values": [-0.0268, -0.0239, -0.0011]}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "values": [-0.0331, -0.0242, -0.0111]}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "values": [-0.0245, -0.0179, -0.0136]}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "values": [-0.0278, -0.0226, -0.0148]}, {"label": "USDCAD", "values": [-0.0069, -0.0036, 0.0105]}, {"label": "USDCHF", "values": [-0.0302, -0.0275, -0.0159]}, {"label": "USDJPY", "values": [-0.0149, 0.0015, 0.0144]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "In money: the pair's next block after a big own move (fade) or a big dollar move (follow), vs the spread", "unit": "daily σ", "ref": 0, "note": "Big = top 10% of moves. Fade = the pair's next-block return signed against the own move; follow = signed with the dollar. Unhedged, gross. Compare with the median round-trip spread, the bar any idea must clear.", "rows": [{"label": "5 min: fade after own", "value": 0.0021, "lo": 0.0016, "hi": 0.0027}, {"label": "5 min: follow after dollar", "value": -0.0003, "lo": -0.0009, "hi": 0.0004}, {"label": "5 min: spread", "value": 0.0358}, {"label": "15 min: fade after own", "value": 0.0024, "lo": 0.0014, "hi": 0.0034}, {"label": "15 min: follow after dollar", "value": 0.0005, "lo": -0.001, "hi": 0.002}, {"label": "15 min: spread", "value": 0.0358}, {"label": "60 min: fade after own", "value": 0.0002, "lo": -0.0047, "hi": 0.0048}, {"label": "60 min: follow after dollar", "value": 0.0008, "lo": -0.0058, "hi": 0.0079}, {"label": "60 min: spread", "value": 0.0356}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Gold and indices vs the dollar factor", "names": ["5-min share", "60-min share"], "unit": "share of variance (point-in-time β)", "note": "Dollar = all 7 majors. Benchmark: 0. The sign of the median β is in the label (gold falls when the dollar rises → negative β).", "rows": [{"label": "GOLD (β -1.02)", "values": [0.2219, 0.2514]}, {"label": "NQ (β -0.57)", "values": [0.1167, 0.1321]}, {"label": "SPX500 (β -0.45)", "values": [0.1248, 0.1452]}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Example: a dollar day in EURUSD: 2022-11-21", "unit": "daily σ from the 00:00 London open", "xlabel": "London hour", "note": "Picked by seed among EURUSD days that moved ≥1σ with ≥90% dollar share. Point-in-time beta 0.85 (prior 20 sessions). Dollar share of the day's move 95%.", "series": [{"name": "EURUSD", "points": [[0.0, -0.0], [0.25, -0.088], [0.5, -0.132], [0.75, -0.166], [1.0, -0.212], [1.25, -0.193], [1.5, -0.329], [1.75, -0.169], [2.0, -0.253], [2.25, -0.46], [2.5, -0.372], [2.75, -0.468], [3.0, -0.481], [3.25, -0.403], [3.5, -0.372], [3.75, -0.369], [4.0, -0.337], [4.25, -0.374], [4.5, -0.487], [4.75, -0.554], [5.0, -0.578], [5.25, -0.589], [5.5, -0.597], [5.75, -0.619], [6.0, -0.574], [6.25, -0.537], [6.5, -0.606], [6.75, -0.701], [7.0, -0.828], [7.25,